{
  "summary": "Reported: Tom Becker (Finance, user_id 4) asked to release a quarantined \"scanned document zip\" he believes came from the office copier. Checked: quarantine for his mailbox. Found: Q-1005 from scanner@docs-share.example, subject \"Scanned document 0931.zip\", received 2026-10-09 20:58 UTC, reason MALWARE, not releasable. The sender is an external domain, not an internal copier, and this matches a common fake-scanner lure. NOT released. Also in quarantine: Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example (invoice, spam, releasable). User did not ask about it, so no action was taken. Also seen: account status is LOCKED with 5 failed sign-ins. The user did not mention it. Might be worth checking sign-in logs in case it is tied to targeting. Needed: security review of the docs-share.example sender, block it org-wide if appropriate, and check whether other users got the same message. Confirm with the user where real copier scans come from (internal scan-to-email address).",
  "reason": "Requested message is marked malware; KB-007/KB-008 require escalation for security review"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the message, but I can't release it. Our email filter flagged the attachment as malware. It also came from an outside address (docs-share.example), not from our office copier. Fake 'scanned document' emails are a common trick, so I've passed it to the security team to review. Scans from our copiers come from an internal address. If you scan the document again, it should arrive normally. If it doesn't, let us know. If you get any other emails like this, please don't open the attachment or forward it. Separately, your account shows as locked after several failed sign-in attempts. If you're having trouble signing in, reply to this ticket and we'll help.",
  "internal_note": "Quarantine for tom.becker: Q-1005 is from scanner@docs-share.example, subject 'Scanned document 0931.zip', reason malware, releasable=false. I did not release it, per KB-007/KB-008. External sender pretending to be a copier, which looks like a phishing/malware lure. Escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation 1). Q-1004 (Harborview invoice, spam, releasable) was not requested, so I took no action on it. The account is locked with 5 failed sign-ins. The user didn't raise it, so I didn't unlock it. Worth checking sign-in logs.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-007",
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
